### The Power of Dynamic HSL Design Tokens

Many design systems struggle when implementing customizable color palettes because hex codes make programmatic opacity manipulation cumbersome.

By leveraging CSS custom properties with raw HSL triplets, our entire interface can re-theme instantly with zero layout shifts:

```css
:root {
  --p: 185 100% 48%; /* Primary cyan/teal */
  --p2: 210 100% 40%; /* Secondary blue */
}

.card-glow {
  background: hsl(210 60% 8% / 0.7);
  border: 1px solid hsl(var(--p) / 0.2);
  box-shadow: 0 10px 40px hsl(var(--p) / 0.1);
}
```

### Key Principles for Cyber Dark Interfaces

1. **Avoid Pure Black**: Use rich deep navy (`hsl(210 100% 4%)`) or charcoal tones for backgrounds. It gives depth and preserves contrast without causing eye fatigue.
2. **Layered Elevation**: Use semi-transparent glass cards with backdrop-blur (`backdrop-filter: blur(24px)`) to create a tangible feeling of physical layers.
3. **Subtle Sheen Highlights**: Add 1px top borders with higher opacity to simulate directional studio lighting from above.

### Micro-Interactions that Delight

Pairing visual feedback with subtle audio clicks elevates a digital portfolio from a static resume into an unforgettable experience.
